# Implementation Plan - Cloudflare Workers & D1 Migration

Adapt the Telegram Mini App Marketplace to run on **Cloudflare Workers** with **Cloudflare D1** (serverless SQL database), enabling instant one-command deployment (`npx wrangler deploy`) with free HTTPS hosting for Telegram Mini Apps.

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
  TelegramApp[Telegram Mini App / Browser Client] -->|HTTPS Fetch| CFWorker[Cloudflare Worker / Hono API]
  CFWorker -->|Static Asset Serving| Dist[Vite Built Dist / Assets]
  CFWorker -->|D1 SQL Queries| CFD1[(Cloudflare D1 Database)]
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Cloudflare Services Used**:
> - **Cloudflare Workers / Assets**: Serves the Vite React frontend static bundle + API endpoints on a global edge network.
> - **Cloudflare D1**: Serverless SQLite-compatible database binding (`env.DB`).
> - **Wrangler**: CLI tool used to test locally (`npx wrangler dev`) and deploy to production (`npx wrangler deploy`).

